{
    "readme": "Reference configuration for remotely-configured event-driven metrics, in the COMPILED shape that clients consume. Each key under metrics is a metric name; source and experiments belong to the metric, and conversions holds one or more {windows, thresholds} groups whose product defines how the metric converts. experiments is a list of literal experiment names: the user-facing config uses regular expressions, but those are expanded at build time, so no client performs pattern matching. searchLike demonstrates the partial product that production retention metrics use — threshold 1 over per-day windows in one group, higher thresholds over range windows in another. There is no state field: presence means the metric converts. Cohort weights are irrelevant here because tests declare enrolled experiments directly via activeExperiments; cohort assignment and enrollment are owned by each experiment type and are out of scope.",
